    "resident": "the Flood-Callers' choir, the drowned they have called up and keep, and Ama Lissa, the Sounder, at the well with the bell-rope in her hands",
    "story": "Under the platform the Builders cut halls down into the peat and lined them with their black stone, and the marsh came in through the floor and stood in the lowest of them as a black pool that has no bottom anybody has found. The Callers call it the well. They have run the bell-rope down to it from the tower, through a shaft in the vault, and the Sounder sits at the edge with the rope across her knees and her feet in the water, waiting for the tide.",
    "unique_object": "the bell-rope coming down through a shaft in the vault into the black water of the well, plaited of rush and hair and knotted its whole length in the bittern's loops of the Lissa weave",
